        "original_id": "d1d40153-bbaa-5632-988d-e37b24557dca",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: \"Rock You Like a Hurricane\", Love at First Sting\n- People: Klaus Meine, Herman Rarebell, Rudolf Schenker\n- Organizations: Scorpions\n- Topics: songwriting, album-track relationships\n\nFacts:\n- In 1984, \"Rock You Like a Hurricane\" was released as the lead single from Love at First Sting.\n- Love at First Sting is the ninth studio album by the German hard rock band Scorpions.\n- Klaus Meine and Herman Rarebell wrote \"Rock You Like a Hurricane\", and Rudolf Schenker composed it.\n- The lyrics of \"Rock You Like a Hurricane\" reference the title of its album, Love at First Sting.\n- Love at First Sting contains \"Rock You Like a Hurricane\", \"Still Loving You\", and \"Big City Nights\", which are three of Scorpions' most famous songs.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "6a379913-d015-5be3-9229-06fc981c7e42",
        "text": "Page: Rock You Like a Hurricane. Sentence: The song was released as the lead single from their ninth studio album, \"Love at First Sting\" (1984).\nPage: Rock You Like a Hurricane. Sentence: It was written by Klaus Meine and Herman Rarebell, and composed by Rudolf Schenker.\nPage: Rock You Like a Hurricane. Sentence: The lyrics of \"Rock You Like a Hurricane\" also reference the title of the album on which it originally appeared – \"Love at First Sting\".\nPage: Love at First Sting. Sentence: Love at First Sting is the ninth studio album by German hard rock band Scorpions.\nPage: Love at First Sting. Sentence: The album contains \"Rock You Like a Hurricane\", \"Still Loving You\", and \"Big City Nights\", three of the band's most famous songs.",
